WEBVTT

00:00:00.100 --> 00:00:04.850
The Crown's Rotten Jewels: How State Corporations Burned Billions.

00:00:04.800 --> 00:00:14.075
Canada operates 43 Crown corporations — state-owned entities shielded from market discipline and insulated from meaningful Parliamentary scrutiny.

00:00:14.075 --> 00:00:26.375
Public Accounts show these entities receive billions in annual appropriations, accumulate staggering pension deficits, and answer to boards appointed by the very governments they should serve independently.

00:00:26.375 --> 00:00:34.775
The Auditor General's Special Examinations — conducted only once per decade — routinely uncover systemic governance failures.

00:00:34.775 --> 00:00:39.062
This is the forensic accounting they don't want Canadians to read.
